		«9/22/05; 12:58:58 AM by JES
			«Fix a bug which could mask errors when a custom error handler script is registered. Only call membership group callbacks if the memberGroupName attribute is defined.
		«5/29/05; 1:44:46 AM by JES
			«If an error handler is registered in the paramtable, allow it to override the default HTML for errors returned by mainResponder.
			«Error handlers are registered by placing an address value named adrErrorHandler in the paramtable (page table), or setting an address value at config.mainResponder.globals.adrErrorHandler. Error handler scripts take a single parameter which is the value of tryError at the time the error occurs.
		«3/17/05; 3:57:45 PM by JES
			«Make call to tcp.equalNames in a try block, since this can fail on servers which aren't connected to the Internet.
		«10/23/04; 1:17:48 AM by JES
			«Respect config.mainResponder.prefs.flMapFirstLevelOfUrlsToManilaSites. If false, then do not map the first level of the path in incoming requests to Manila sites. Default is to preserve existing behavior in existing installs, and to not map to Manila sites in new installs. (See mainResponder.init and mainResponder.install.)
		«9/16/04; 2:11:44 AM by JES
			«Fix a bug in latin-to-mac translation when parsing POST args where more than one argument has the same name.
